<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="048" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>AI code-set mapping proposals (admin-confirmed)</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Proposal generation plus admin-only confirm endpoints; nothing is applied without confirmation, so the risk is bounded to the confirm route's authorization.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Small service + two routes reusing the Finance filter and an existing facade member.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>047</deps>
    <tags>bff, ai, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement FR-22's admin action: for matter types and practice areas with no default code set, the AI proposes a code set; an admin confirms each proposal, and only a confirmed proposal writes sprk_defaultbillingcodeset. Also plug the per-line AI suggestion (FR-22 step 4, flagged for review) into 047's hook. Choose the smallest surface: BFF endpoints only; any UI is an escalation.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in BFF endpoints, Finance authorization filters and embeddings. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>GET proposals returns, for every unmapped sprk_mattertype_ref / sprk_practicearea_ref row, a proposed code set with a score and short rationale; POST confirm writes the mapping for one row after an admin check; 047's suggestion hook returns a flagged suggestion for a line whose record has no mapping; nothing is ever applied without confirmation.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-22: "An admin action asks the AI to propose code-set mappings for unmapped matter types / practice areas; the admin confirms each (no mapping is applied unconfirmed)." Brief: endpoint + model-driven view, or a Rule Review-style list — choose the smallest. Tables (018): sprk_billingcodeset (name, body, version, source URL), sprk_defaultbillingcodeset lookup on sprk_mattertype_ref and sprk_practicearea_ref. After task 029, SpaarkeMaster solution source is edited only by serial tasks (project CLAUDE.md, 2026-10-15 pipeline directive) and this task's tags exclude frontend, so no form, view or page is built here; the admin's existing model-driven form for the reference tables already lets an admin set the lookup by hand.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Coding/CodeSetProposalService.cs (+ interface; implements 047's AI-suggestion hook)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/CodeSetMappingEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:376-377 (shared Finance mapping call site: one line)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:154 (FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege — table privilege asked of Dataverse as the caller)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IInvoiceAi.cs:81 (GenerateEmbeddingAsync)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:30-33</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Coding/CodeSetProposalServiceTests.cs; tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/CodeSetMappingEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="047" status="required">CodeSetResolver and its AI-suggestion hook interface.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-22">No mapping is written except by the confirm route acting on one admin-confirmed row. The per-line suggestion is used only for that line's coding, recorded as a finding input for review, and never persisted as a mapping.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-028">Routes under /api/finance with RequireAuthorization, an endpoint filter, then RequireEbillingEnabled(). Confirm: caller must hold Write on the target reference table (FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege, e.g. prvWritesprk_mattertype_ref) — the caller's own Dataverse rights decide, not an app role. Proposals GET: the same check (proposals are admin data).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-52 / ADR-013">Proposals use IInvoiceAi.GenerateEmbeddingAsync (reference-row name and description versus code-set name, body and description); no new Action and no prompt in C#. If embeddings cannot rank sensibly, escalate rather than add an Action.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Stable codes: ebilling.codeset.forbidden (403), ebilling.codeset.not_found (404 for an unknown reference row or code set), ebilling.codeset.already_mapped (409 when the row gained a mapping since the proposal).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Finance endpoints and authorization</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor STANDARD. Read 047's hook interface and notes; re-read FinanceModule.cs and EndpointMappingExtensions.cs before editing.</step>
    <step order="1">CodeSetProposalService.ProposeAsync: list unmapped reference rows of both tables; embed each and every active code set (cache code-set embeddings per request); return the best set with score and runner-up.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the 047 hook: for a line whose core record's matter type and practice area are both unmapped, return the proposal for that matter type (or practice area) flagged as an AI suggestion.</step>
    <step order="3">Endpoints: GET /api/finance/code-set-mappings/proposals; POST /api/finance/code-set-mappings/{table}/{id}/confirm with body {codeSetId} where table is mattertype or practicearea; the confirm re-reads the row and refuses with 409 if it is already mapped.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: proposal ranking on fixtures; mapped rows excluded; confirm writes exactly one lookup; 403 without the privilege; 409 on race; 503 flag off; 401 unauthenticated; hook returns flagged suggestion only when unmapped.</step>
    <step order="5">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests ledger for the two routes; build, test, publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations (no UI built, privilege names used) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner wants an admin screen (model-driven view, list or page) for proposals, STOP before building it: SpaarkeMaster solution source is reserved for serial tasks after 029 and this task carries no frontend tag — the UI needs its own task or must ride on a deploy task (112).</trigger>
    <trigger>If embedding similarity proposes an obviously wrong set for the seeded reference data (for example Bankruptcy for a litigation matter type), STOP and propose a prompted Action instead of adding one silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No mapping-proposal capability exists; the reference tables' model-driven forms allow manual mapping only. FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege and IInvoiceAi.GenerateEmbeddingAsync are reused.</existing>
    <extension>047's CodeSetResolver is extended through its hook rather than duplicated; the two routes need their own endpoint file per the brief's endpoint convention.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-22 fails: unmapped matter types silently fall back to the Litigation default with no AI suggestion flagged and no admin action to fix the mapping.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Services/Finance/Coding/CodeSetProposalService.cs, Api/Finance/CodeSetMappingEndpoints.cs, one line each in EndpointMappingExtensions.cs and FinanceModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">CodeSetProposalServiceTests.cs, CodeSetMappingEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">GET proposals lists every unmapped matter type and practice area with a proposed code set and score; mapped rows are excluded; nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST confirm by a caller holding Write on the reference table sets sprk_defaultbillingcodeset on exactly that row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: caller without the privilege → 403 ebilling.codeset.forbidden and nothing written; row already mapped → 409 ebilling.codeset.already_mapped; unknown ids → 404; flag off → 503 ebilling.disabled; unauthenticated → 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no code path writes a mapping without the confirm route (grep for writes of sprk_defaultbillingcodeset finds only the confirm handler).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The coding hook returns a suggestion flagged for review only when both the matter type and the practice area of the line's core record are unmapped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-22 (admin action sentence). Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:376-377. Core records reach the reference rows through their sprk_mattertype / sprk_practicearea lookup columns (target tables sprk_mattertype_ref / sprk_practicearea_ref).
Completed 2026-10-16. Full notes: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/048-code-set-mapping-proposals.md. No UI built; privilege names are mixed case (prvWritesprk_MatterType_Ref / prvWritesprk_PracticeArea_Ref, live names); ADR-010 ceiling 166 to 165 (ICodeSetSuggestionProvider gained its second implementation); publish-size delta +0.01 MB vs branch base (+0.15 MB branch vs fresh master); no live seeding needed. OPEN OWNER QUESTION (trigger 2): embeddings propose an obviously wrong set for 3 of 11 seeded reference rows (Commercial, Mergers and Acquisitions, Commercial Transactions); see notes section 3 for options (accept, minimum score, prompted Action). Adversarial pass not run (sub-agent limit).
rework: none task 048</notes>

